n actual, directly observed node reboot (boot_id change, fresh uptime, service and swap state recovered without manual intervention). Operational hygiene is high: the only non-final-outcome mutations were a brief, fully reverted modprobe/rmmod diagnostic and a memory-pressure test process that was cleanly terminated, with no residue, failed services, or unsafe exposure in the final state.\",\"limitations\":[\"No pre-existing disk-backed swap was present on node1, so 'preferred over disk-backed swap' could only be verified via the configured priority value rather than an observed real contest between zram and a disk swap device.\",\"One functional-test command (cmd-38d344155a9d427b) returned a proxy timeout rather than a clean completion, though the subsequent commands confirm the intended memory-pressure effect occurred and was cleaned up.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"swap-size","requirement":"At least 512 MB of compressed in-memory (zram) swap configured on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"init-zram-swapping fixes zram0 disksize at 671088640 bytes (640 MiB), well above the 512 MB floor. swapon --show and /proc/swaps confirm /dev/zram0 active at 640M with lz4 compression algorithm selected.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0061f103fb524c3e","cmd-aabc1b2fa64e4c36","cmd-cea57645f0aa4178"]},{"id":"swap-at-boot","requirement":"Swap is active at boot (persists across restart), not just currently running","status":"satisfied","summary":"zram-config.service is enabled and WantedBy=multi-user.target. A real reboot was performed: pre-restart baseline (boot_id b185f188...) was captured, the node was rebooted natively (connection refused observed mid-downtime confirming an actual disruption), and post-restart state shows a new boot_id (9faea938...), fresh uptime of 0 minutes, and zram0 swap automatically active at 640M/priority 100/lz4 with the service enabled+active, with no manual re-application. This matches the fixed lifecycle boot-identity change (before_pr